🎯 Learning Path

Follow the courses in this order:

HTML
  ↓
CSS
  ↓
JavaScript
  ↓
Bootstrap
  ↓
jQuery

Prerequisites

No previous programming experience is required.
Basic computer knowledge and a willingness to learn are enough to get started.

🛠️ Tools You Can Use

Code Editor: Visual Studio Code

Browser: Google Chrome, Firefox, or Microsoft Edge

Version Control: Git & GitHub

💻 Practice Projects

As you progress through the courses, try building projects such as:

Personal Portfolio Website

Landing Page

Login & Registration Form

Calculator

To-Do List

Image Gallery

Responsive Navbar

Product Card

Weather App

Interactive Quiz

📈 Goal

By completing these courses and projects, you will build a strong foundation in frontend web development and be able to create responsive, interactive, and user-friendly websites.

⭐ Contributing

If you find an error or have a useful example, feel free to contribute by creating a pull request.

